+  // helium-fork r8.4: the address bar has exactly one mode -- left. r8.3
+  // sealed the *bounds* half of Helium's "centered location bar"
+  // (ToolbarView::GetCenteredLocationBarBounds) but left this, the text
+  // alignment half, still riding the pref. With the pref on, a resting field
+  // put the domain 50pt to the right of the site-settings icon: the Arc band
+  // sizes the resting omnibox to text width + 100pt of forgiveness slack
+  // (LocationBarView::Layout), and centring inside that box splits the slack
+  // in two. On a blank new tab, where there is no text, the same arm centred
+  // the *placeholder* in the composer's box. Both read as "the URL has a hole
+  // in front of it" -- reported 2026-08-21 with the pref True in the profile.
+  //
+  // Sealed the same way as the bounds half: the pref stays registered (no
+  // migration), the switch is gone. Anything that wants centred omnibox text
+  // back has to reinstate both halves deliberately.
+  SetHorizontalAlignment(gfx::ALIGN_LEFT);
+  set_placeholder_text_draw_flags(gfx::Canvas::TEXT_ALIGN_LEFT);
